        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Genetics rulings</p>
        <h3>Defeating genetic-testing defenses</h3>
        <p>Defendants increasingly argue a cancer “runs in the family” or that a mutation — not asbestos — explains the diagnosis. Louisiana courts have ruled in cases handled by Landry &amp; Swarr that:</p>
        <ul class="ticks ticks--light">
          <li>Defendants cannot force invasive genetic testing based on speculation</li>
          <li>Genetics witnesses cannot stretch beyond their medical qualifications to shift blame away from asbestos exposure</li>
        </ul>
